+    * Each member cut from a base of its own (:func:`_own_base_cut`): the commit it was cut
+      from. A member's branch brings in what that base held, from below its cut point, and
+      that is the work of the bundles it was ordered after, which ``d`` is ordered after
+      too — also when this run neither built nor carried them, or their work is on the base
+      under commits of its own (a squash or rebase merge). Not when that base holds work of
+      a finished id of ``rejected`` (name → ``(directory, the head its CLOSED PR
+      reports)``, :func:`_finished_head`): its PR was turned down after the member was built
+      on it, so that work stays unowned and the base is refused. Such a member is carried
+      only when its edge to that id is one the not-clean cascade does not follow, a
+      ``Conflicts with`` or ``Depends on (merged)`` one (:func:`_cascade_not_clean`).
