+def _finished_after(cfg: Config, graph: Mapping[str, tuple[Path, int]],
+                    carried: Mapping[str, str],
+                    conflicts: Mapping[str, Collection[str]]) -> dict[str, set[str]]:
+    """For each finished bundle of ``graph`` (wave -1, :func:`_bundle_bases`), the finished
+    ``Conflicts with`` partners an earlier run built before it (#728): those whose work is
+    below the commit it was cut from, its recorded stack-base tip
+    (``publish.read_stack_base_tip``). For a partner the run carried (``carried``: name →
+    its head) that is some of its own work — the non-merge commits its head adds over the
+    target base and its own recorded tip, as :func:`integrate.build_bundle_base` counts a
+    member's own work — so one built after the bundle is never named. For one with no
+    patch, it is all that its own recorded tip added over the base, if anything: what that
+    one was built on, which the bundle's branch then brings too. A bundle with no recorded
+    tip (built on the base itself) names none.
+
+    Read in the bundle's target checkout as the run fetched it. A commit or a base that clone
+    does not have names nothing (at worst the dependent's base is then refused for work no
+    member owns, never built on unrelated work); a git failure raises
+    :class:`integrate.IntegrationError`."""
+    after: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
+    for m, (mp, wave) in graph.items():
